            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p>Magicians are incredibly powerful people. They just might not realize exactly how powerful they are and they probably don&rsquo;t consider the consequences of their power.Whether they know they have such power at their fingertips or not it is this sense of power that the Magician seeks.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Magicians might not always look for their power the right places, but they&rsquo;ll probably be aware that they have an uncanny ability to get whatever they want, even if it doesn&rsquo;t happen all the time.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The truth is Magicians could get what they want all the time too. It&rsquo;s just that they are probably not aligning themselves congruently in some cases to their goals which means that they can cancel out and neutralize their creations or even manifest something that is not good for them.</p>
                <p>For example, if a Magician desires a loving and committed relationship, but they are insecure inside and don&rsquo;t believe that such a relationship is possible for them, then they won&rsquo;t manifest the outcome they desire - because they&rsquo;ll cancel this opportunity out with the belief that it&rsquo;s not possible.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This ability to create anything they focus on is why it&rsquo;s essential for Magicians to keep on top of their mindset and stay it positive.It's also crucial for them to work on adjusting their limiting beliefs so that they align with their goals.If they do this, then that's when the magic really starts to happen.</p>
                <p><strong>Magicians In Love</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians make incredible partners if they can learn to open up and connect and are fully committed to being with the person, they are with.And if they are genuinely in love with somebody and they believe that they are loveable, then Magicians can use their powers of manifestation to create the perfect relationship in their eyes.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Magician is insecure in love, they&rsquo;d have to heal that issue first before they can manifest the romance of the century!The same applies to pretty much anything else that the Magician wishes to manifest.</p>
                <p><strong>Diverse Characters</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians are diverse in personality because of the nature of their primary focus which is power.They can apply their power in any way imaginable - for better or for worse.They are also usually highly intellectual, spiritual, aware of things that others might not even notice and can also be unwittingly intimidating at times.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Connecting With Others</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians do tend to find it difficult to connect with others because they are so different from others and are naturally dominant. They often find it difficult to understand that others don&rsquo;t have such advanced abilities or that they might not even desire to have such skills.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s difficult to assign the Magician to a specific character trait, because they can essentially take on all of them, depending upon their interests.But they will all have the same needs, and challenges that come from the driving force within them.</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side.Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do, or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires, or reach our fullest potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Highly Complex</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians are complex creatures. They have so many facets, depths, and visions that it&rsquo;s highly likely that the most profound aspects of the Magicians inner world will be wholly individual and exclusive to each Magician.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Magicians tend to have less generic traits overall than the other archetypes, but one thing is for sure; if they are aware that they have such power and potential, they'll probably consider themselves to be nothing without it.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This knowledge might manifest in a secret fear of losing their power in some Magicians.It can also show up in a fear of losing whatever they have created with their power.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>For example; If a Magician has used their power to become an influencer in some way, they might fear irrelevancy.If they have built a business, they might fear losing their business.</p>
                <p><strong>The Need To Choose Between Right And Wrong</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians also secretly find it challenging to connect with others.Some might not even like people too much - even if they might never admit it to themselves, let alone others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They might find others to be weak, flighty, superficial, optimistic, naive. They might find others weak because the Magician has a lot of exceptional character and personality traits and a high level of intellect (and sometimes a considerable ego too).They sometimes don&rsquo;t realize that others don&rsquo;t have the same advantages as them or that there are different ways to enjoy life and feel fulfilled that are not based on attaining power.And so, Magicians can feel impatient, confused or frustrated with others.They are also far too busy using their power to be concerned too much about the needs of others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s this indifference towards connecting with others, and even sometimes a lack of empathy toward other people, combined with the Magicians desire for power and egotistical ways (in some cases) that can sometimes lead the Magician to struggle to understand what&rsquo;s right and wrong.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>For a Caregiver archetype, people need help, for a Lover they need love, for a creator they need expression these are all examples of empathy based, human traits that are the epitome of humanity.But power, well, it can be achieved with or without compassion, which means it can be used for good or bad.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Occasionally Unaware Of Their Impact</strong></p>
                <p>Because of the lack of compassion that some Magician&rsquo;s experience they might not be consciously aware of the impact of how they use their powers and even if they are aware, they may keep on doing their thing regardless of its effect on society. Whereas a Caregiver, Lover or Creator along with some other archetypes would stop doing something if it did not serve humanity well.</p>
                <p>This means that the Magician has to pay attention to understanding the fine line between right and wrong.Secretly, the Magician has probably crossed both sides as they have begun to explore their powers, but one of their most significant challenges is to stay within boundaries.</p>
                <p>Magicians will always have to grapple between when to use their power or not, and also whether their use of their power serves for the good or the bad. This problem reduces if they have already been preconditioned to one side or the other by their genetics, history, family, and upbringing but it can rear its head frequently in a Magicians life and is their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s not so much how the Magician grows and develops as a result of stepping into their power, which is the case for all other archetypes, but more so that the Magician has his or her power already.So, their challenge is in having the foresight to understand the consequences and quality of life they and others will have at the cost of their decisions, including their moral stance. As we&rsquo;ve already highlighted, this is a complex task with an extremely fine line to work with.</p>
                <p>It is your destiny as a Magician to feel the wonders that your magnificence can bring to the world but to attain this experience you must first overcome the hurdles that are preventing you from completely stepping into your power.You&rsquo;ll learn more about how your power can create or destruct in a heartbeat, and you can start to work on addressing these challenges through the process of individuation and also shadow work.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Check out The Premium Archetype report to learn more about your Shadow Self and how to get started on the journey to individuation.</p>
