            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">
                <p><strong>Extremely Intuitive</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians are intuitive to a fault.  Even if they have not consciously acknowledged this intuition, they’ll probably use it a lot. The Magicians intuition is their guiding light and has probably helped them out of many challenges and has led them to plenty of wonderful experiences throughout their life.</p>
                <p><strong>Highly Intellectual</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians are also incredibly intelligent, they usually also develop great knowledge and wisdom about whatever they are interested in and focused on throughout life.  This intelligence and wisdom make the Magician a fascinating and unique character, especially when combined with their other personality traits.</p>
                <p><strong>Disciplined</strong></p>
                <p>When a Magician is focused on a specific outcome, they are extremely disciplined.  They are laser-focused and will follow projects through in the same sharp manner - right to the very end.  Unfortunately, though, they don’t always apply this discipline to their personal growth, personal awareness or habits, which is where their potential for real power lies.</p>
                <p><strong>A Great Visionary</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians are the greatest visionaries of all archetypes. They can visualize things that most people couldn’t even comprehend, and then when they have mastered their power, they can bring their visions into manifestation too.  It’s hardly surprising that some people feel unnerved when they are around a Magician.  Such power, discipline, wisdom, and insight can put even the most confident person on edge!</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Egotistical</strong></p>
                <p>Because the Magicians primary focus is power, it’s easy to see that they probably have to work hard to manage their ego (or at least they should).  If they are not careful their ego can lead the Magician into trouble and strife that can be difficult to get out of, or they could lose people around them who they love the most. </p>
                <p>The Magician will have to work hard at applying humility to all things, because an ego driven by a power which is easy to attain can easily lead the Magician down the pathway to darkness, instead of enjoying lighthearted fulfillment and the joys of life.</p>
                <p><strong>Cares Little About Connecting With Others</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians don’t deal with others too well.  Some Magicians don’t care too much about others at all, instead, seeing them as a tool to get what they need.  If a Magician is interested in leading a fulfilling life, they will do well to use some of their ‘magic’ to learn how to connect with others - everybody needs a sense of connection, including the Magician. </p>
                <p><strong>Can Be Manipulative</strong></p>
                <p>A Magician who can be egotistical, powerful and has little concern for others can easily manipulate to get what they want, and they’ll probably achieve their goals in doing so.  If a Magician hasn’t developed morals to protect them from heading down this road, then it’s likely that a Magician can manipulate.  It’s not an attractive quality, nor does it promote trust or a sense of connection, so if you are a Magician and you know you have the potential to manipulate others, but also want to lead a fulfilling life, now’s the time to mend your ways.</p>
                <p><strong>Magicians Are Highly Critical Of Themselves And Others</strong></p>
                <p>Magicians see life from a different perspective than most, they often have an above average intellect and sense of wisdom - and if they’ve managed to harness their powers, they’ll probably have an above average sense of confidence too - Which means that they can pick holes in others all day long. </p>
                <p>They have high standards which are often difficult for others to meet and the standards they have for themselves are also extremely high. In some cases, such high expectations can cause the Magician to sabotage their projects because they cannot meet their standards and then learn not to trust their abilities.  It’s a vicious cycle that doesn’t help the Magician.</p>
                <p>If the Magicians ease the pressure on everybody, they will empower others and themselves to be better.</p>
